FILE 3 — vllm/config.py  (or vllm/v1/config.py — wherever VllmConfig lives)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Add a new config dataclass (can live in a new file vllm/offload_config.py):

    # vllm/offload_config.py
    from __future__ import annotations
    from dataclasses import dataclass, field
    from typing import Optional

    @dataclass
    class OffloadVllmConfig:
        \"\"\"
        Configuration for the offload_package KV offloading integration.

        Pass via:
            engine_args = EngineArgs(
                ...
                offload_config=OffloadVllmConfig(
                    gpu_budget_blocks=1000,
                    num_cpu_slots=4096,
                    num_staging_slots=64,
                    interval_tokens=16,
                ),
            )
        \"\"\"

        # Max GPU pages allowed to stay resident; excess are offloaded to CPU.
        gpu_budget_blocks: int = 1000

        # Capacity of the pinned CPU offload buffer (in pages).
        num_cpu_slots: int = 4096

        # GPU staging pages (reserved at the tail of the GPU cache tensor).
        # Rule of thumb: ~2x the max sparse_len budget in blocks.
        num_staging_slots: int = 64

        # Eviction fires every this many decoded tokens.
        # Must be a multiple of page_size.
        interval_tokens: int = 16

        # PagedEvictionScorer knobs.
        scorer_decay: float = 1.0
        scorer_head_reduction: str = "mean"   # "mean" | "min"

Add ``offload_config: Optional[OffloadVllmConfig] = None`` to VllmConfig.

Register in EngineArgs.__init__ / from_cli_args as needed.

